message: "If you use this analysis, its data or its analysis plan, please cite it as below."
title: "The diabetes-TB gap in India's States: code, extracted data, outputs, analysis plan and online material"
abstract: >-
  Code, extracted data, outputs, online material and an analysis plan time-stamped in a
  public repository before estimation, for a State-level analysis of the TB-diabetes care
  cascade in India: screening of people notified with TB for diabetes, diabetes identified among those screened relative to a benchmark built
  from the NFHS-5 State prevalence of raised or treated blood sugar, and initiation of
  anti-diabetic treatment. It counts the people with TB and diabetes expected among those
  not screened and among those screened but not identified, gives tiers rather than
  ranks, classes each unit's shortfall as screening-led or identification-led, and tests
  whether identification follows the diabetes burden across units. It uses published,
  aggregate India TB Report tables (data years 2018, 2019, 2021, 2022 and 2023) and
  NFHS-5 fact sheets. Observational; no causal estimates.
